 "cells": [
  {"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{},"source":["# Capstone — Content Refresh Prioritization Research Paper\n","\n","Public-safe research artifact built from the FlyRank ML Internship dataset. The paper asks whether observed content and search-performance signals can help prioritize pages for human review for a possible content refresh."]},
  {"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{},"source":["## 1. Question\n","\n","### Research question\n","Can observed content and search-performance signals be used to prioritize pages for human review for a possible content refresh?\n","\n","### Decision supported\n","The output supports a reviewer deciding which pages to examine first. It is decision-support, not an automatic refresh decision, and it does not claim that refreshing a page will improve future search performance."]},
  {"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{},"outputs":[],"source":["from pathlib import Path\n","import pandas as pd\n","\n","DATA_PATH = Path(\"../../data/raw/content_refresh_anonymized.csv\")\n","df = pd.read_csv(DATA_PATH)\n","print(\"Rows:\", len(df))\n","print(\"Columns:\", len(df.columns))\n","print(df[[\"content_id\", \"client_id\", \"trend_direction\"]].head())"]},
  {"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{},"source":["## 2. Data\n","\n","The modeling work uses the anonymized content-refresh slice of the FlyRank ML Internship dataset. The file contains 30,000 page-level observations. Each row represents a content-page observation with search, content, and recent performance attributes.\n","\n","Client identifiers are used only to create a grouped validation split and are not disclosed. Outcome fields are excluded from predictive features. No client names, private queries, or private URLs are included in this artifact.\n","\n","The analysis uses the development/test framing established earlier in the track: a March 2026 development window and a sealed June 2026 outcome/test window where applicable. This notebook reports the measured Week-5 grouped evaluation rather than implying causal refresh success."]},
  {"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{},"outputs":[],"source":["print(\"Unique clients:\", df[\"client_id\"].nunique())\n","print(\"Target distribution:\")\n","print(df[\"trend_direction\"].value_counts(dropna=False))\n","\n","excluded = {\"trend_direction\", \"trend_pct\"}\n","print(\"Excluded outcome-derived columns:\", sorted(excluded & set(df.columns)))"]},
  {"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{},"source":["## 3. Methodology\n","\n","### Target\n","For the Week-5 model, `trend_direction == down` was treated as the attention-positive class. This is a proxy for prioritization; it is not a label for successful content refresh.\n","\n","### Features\n","The Logistic Regression used search volume, competition level, CPC, word count, character count, 90-day impressions, clicks, pageviews, sessions, content age, and CTR. `trend_direction` and `trend_pct` were excluded because they are outcome information.\n","\n","### Model\n","Logistic Regression was selected because it is simple, interpretable, and appropriate for a first classification model. Numeric inputs were imputed and standardized; `competition_level` was imputed and one-hot encoded.\n","\n","### Validation\n","The final evaluation used an 80/20 split grouped by `client_id`, with random seed 42. The recorded split contained 23,837 training rows and 6,163 test rows, with 25 training clients and 7 test clients and zero client overlap.\n","\n","### Baseline\n","The Week-4 baseline was a simple rule based on observed content age, CTR, and 90-day impressions. The model and baseline were compared on the same evaluation set using Average Precision and ROC-AUC."]},
  {"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{},"outputs":[],"source":["from sklearn.model_selection import GroupShuffleSplit\n","from sklearn.compose import ColumnTransformer\n","from sklearn.pipeline import Pipeline\n","from sklearn.preprocessing import OneHotEncoder, StandardScaler\n","from sklearn.impute import SimpleImputer\n","from sklearn.linear_model import LogisticRegression\n","from sklearn.metrics import average_precision_score, roc_auc_score\n","\n","target = \"trend_direction\"\n","positive = (df[target] == \"down\").astype(int)\n","\n","feature_cols = [\n","    \"search_volume\", \"competition_level\", \"cpc\", \"word_count\",\n","    \"char_count\", \"impressions_90d\", \"clicks_90d\",\n","    \"pageviews_90d\", \"sessions_90d\", \"content_age_days\",\n","    \"ctr\"\n","]\n","feature_cols = [c for c in feature_cols if c in df.columns]\n","X = df[feature_cols].copy()\n","groups = df[\"client_id\"]\n","\n","gss = GroupShuffleSplit(n_splits=1, test_size=0.20, random_state=42)\n","train_idx, test_idx = next(gss.split(X, positive, groups=groups))\n","X_train, X_test = X.iloc[train_idx], X.iloc[test_idx]\n","y_train, y_test = positive.iloc[train_idx], positive.iloc[test_idx]\n","\n","num_cols = X.select_dtypes(include=\"number\").columns.tolist()\n","cat_cols = [c for c in X.columns if c not in num_cols]\n","preprocess = ColumnTransformer([\n","    (\"num\", Pipeline([\n","        (\"impute\", SimpleImputer(strategy=\"median\")),\n","        (\"scale\", StandardScaler())\n","    ]), num_cols),\n","    (\"cat\", Pipeline([\n","        (\"impute\", SimpleImputer(strategy=\"most_frequent\")),\n","        (\"onehot\", OneHotEncoder(handle_unknown=\"ignore\"))\n","    ]), cat_cols)\n,"] )\n","\n","model = Pipeline([\n","    (\"prep\", preprocess),\n","    (\"model\", LogisticRegression(max_iter=1000, random_state=42))\n,"])\n","model.fit(X_train, y_train)\n","p_model = model.predict_proba(X_test)[:, 1]\n","\n","model_ap = average_precision_score(y_test, p_model)\n","model_auc = roc_auc_score(y_test, p_model)\n","print(\"Training rows:\", len(train_idx))\n","print(\"Test rows:\", len(test_idx))\n","print(\"Train clients:\", groups.iloc[train_idx].nunique())\n","print(\"Test clients:\", groups.iloc[test_idx].nunique())\n","print(\"Client overlap:\", len(set(groups.iloc[train_idx]) & set(groups.iloc[test_idx])))\n","print(\"Measured Logistic Regression AP:\", round(model_ap, 4))\n","print(\"Measured Logistic Regression ROC-AUC:\", round(model_auc, 4))"]},
  {"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{},"source":["## 4. Results (vs baseline)\n","\n","The Week-5 evaluation measured higher performance for Logistic Regression than the Week-4 baseline on the same grouped evaluation design. These are observed validation metrics, not guarantees of future refresh outcomes."]},
  {"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{},"outputs":[],"source":["# Recorded Week-4 baseline results from the executed Week-5 comparison.\n","baseline_ap = 0.4974\n","baseline_auc = 0.4644\n","\n","results = pd.DataFrame({\n","    \"method\": [\"W04 baseline rule\", \"Logistic Regression\"],\n","    \"average_precision\": [baseline_ap, model_ap],\n","    \"roc_auc\": [baseline_auc, model_auc]\n","})\n","print(results.to_string(index=False))\n","print(\"\\nPreviously recorded Week-5 model values: AP=0.5582, ROC-AUC=0.5621\")"]},
  {"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{},"source":["### Interpretation\n","The executed Week-5 comparison recorded Average Precision of 0.5582 for Logistic Regression versus 0.4974 for the baseline, and ROC-AUC of 0.5621 versus 0.4644. The measured direction favors the model under the evaluated split. Because the target is a proxy and the evidence is observational, the result supports prioritization for human review rather than an automatic refresh claim."]},
  {"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{},"source":["## 5. Limitations\n","\n","1. `trend_direction` is a proxy target; it is not the same as confirmed refresh need or refresh success.\n","2. The analysis measures associations and does not establish that a content change causes improved search performance.\n","3. Search intent, competitor changes, content quality, and business priorities are not fully represented.\n","4. Results come from one grouped validation design and may differ on other clients or periods.\n","5. Model performance is moderate; neither metric indicates perfect ranking quality.\n","6. The output should not automatically publish, rewrite, delete, redirect, or change production SEO settings."]},
  {"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{},"source":["## 6. Ranked recommendations\n","\n","### 1 — Refresh first\n","Prioritize pages showing multiple observed refresh signals, especially relatively stale pages that still have meaningful search visibility. A human reviewer must verify content quality and search intent before acting.\n","\n","### 2 — Monitor next\n","Review pages with moderate evidence, such as visibility combined with relatively weak CTR, before deciding whether a refresh is justified.\n","\n","### 3 — Leave for now\n","Do not prioritize pages when the available signals provide limited evidence for immediate action. Revisit when the observed signals change.\n","\n","The action queue is decision-support only. It should not be treated as proof that a recommended refresh will improve performance."]},
  {"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{},"outputs":[],"source":["recommendations = pd.DataFrame({\n","    \"rank\": [1, 2, 3],\n","    \"action\": [\"refresh_first\", \"monitor_next\", \"leave_for_now\"],\n","    \"reason_code\": [\n","        \"multiple observed refresh signals\",\n","        \"moderate evidence from visibility and CTR signals\",\n","        \"limited evidence for immediate action\"\n","    ],\n","    \"human_review\": [True, True, True]\n","})\n","print(recommendations.to_string(index=False))"]},
  {"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{},"source":["## 7. Artifacts the paper embeds\n","\n","The deployed paper uses the model-vs-baseline metrics above and a visual comparison of Average Precision and ROC-AUC. The final artifact intentionally uses public-safe aggregate numbers rather than exposing individual content, clients, queries, or URLs."]},
  {"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{},"outputs":[],"source":["# Paper-ready metrics table.\n","paper_metrics = results.copy()\n","paper_metrics.to_csv(\"../../work/outputs/capstone_metrics.csv\", index=False)\n","print(\"Saved: work/outputs/capstone_metrics.csv\")\n","print(paper_metrics.to_string(index=False))"]},
